All these days we were using frappe docker 2022 single server setup. My existing 2022 instance all work fine till date. Thanks to the frappe docker community. I noticed 2023 upgrade in frappe docker which sounded to me more flexible in terms of upgrades in future especially the assets. We setup a new production instance based on the new changes outlined in Single server Example Everything works like a charm except for the two issues. All the links in emails such as password reset, unsubscribe email link, document link are added with port 8000 like site1.mydomain.com:8000 :api/method/frappe.email.queue.unsubscribe?.. Issuing pdf print is keeps spinning without any output. Also when Attach document print is enabled in the email, the email send ends with timeout error. And again port 8000 is added in the stylesheet get_response_content = <function get_response_content at 0x7f35b1bb76d0> href="http://bluemaple.lmnas.com:8000/assets/frappe/dist/css/print.bundle.V2BFJYQM.css" rel="stylesheet" type="text/css"/>

		<style>
		@media screen {
	.print-format-gutter {
		background-color: #d1d8dd;
		padding: 30px 0px;
	}
	.print-format {
		background-color: white;
		border-radius: 8px;
		max-width: 8.3in;
